In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.
By the right of Muhammad the Prophet, I ask You;
by the right of "There is no god but God," and His might and the Throne <note>the Empyrean</note>
and its vastness; and the Tablet <note>the Preserved Tablet of divine decrees</note> and its protection;
and the Pen and its flow; and the Bridge <note>the hair-thin path over Hell</note>
and its thinness; and the Balance <note>the scale of deeds</note> and its lightness;

<column-break/>

and by the right of Gabriel and his faithfulness; and
Michael and his message; and Israfil
and his trumpet-blast; and Azrael
and his grasp <note>of souls</note>; and Ridwan <note>guardian of Heaven</note> and his paradise;
and Malik <note>guardian of Hell</note> and his stern angels; and Adam and
his purity; and Luqman <note>the Wise</note> and his awe;
and Idris and his elevation; and Noah
